#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Slack CLI.

The same file is installed under three names. As command, it only reads, and
asks for approval to post. As describe and action, which Claude never runs, it
says what a post asks for, and posts.

command reads with SLACK_TOKEN, a user token (xoxp-) from an app created with
manifest.json, and describe with the same token, kept in the Keychain as
slack-cli. action posts with the user token of a second app, which can only
post, kept in the Keychain as slack-write-cli.
"""

